{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["Va-yichad — from the root חדות, as in: עוז וחדוה. Thus every word whose initial letter is one of בג\"ד כפ\"ת that is derived from a form with a hatef-lamed — a verb whose final [letter] carries a dagesh — [takes a dagesh]. From בכה: ויבך. From פתה: ויפת בסתר לבי. יפת אלהים ליפת. Do not add to His words. From שבה: וישב."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The lemma reads ויחד but Rashbam derives it from חדות; the bracketed [חדות] replaces the manuscript reading חדה. The phrase 'a verb whose final [letter] carries a dagesh' translates פעל שסופם דגשים literally; the referent of 'their/their final' is ambiguous but concerns the dagesh in the בג\"ד כפ\"ת letter after a sheva-naḥ under the preceding guttural."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:57.497580118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}